# Integer32 literal above the maximum

Verifies an int32 literal one past the 32-bit maximum is rejected with a
compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
const too_large: int32 = 2147483648
print(too_large)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `2147483648` for type `int32`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 25, end: 35 }

<<< exit
1
